@@ -0,0 +1,158 @@
+# Threshold Feature Implementation Summary
+
+## Overview
+Added `--threshold` option to `frai eval` that allows users to specify minimum metric score thresholds, enabling the evaluation command to gate CI pipelines on metric quality.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. CLI Package (frai-cli/src/index.ts)
+
+#### Interface Update
+- Added `threshold?: string[]` to `EvalOptions` interface
+
+#### New Functions
+- `parseThresholds(thresholdStrs: string[] | undefined)`: Parses and validates threshold strings
+  - Format: `<metric>=<number>` (e.g., `exact_match=0.9`)
+  - Validates metric IDs against whitelist: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`
+  - Validates min values are between 0 and 1
+  - Exits with code 2 for malformed/invalid thresholds
+  - Lists valid metric IDs in error messages
+
+#### Command Update
+- Added `--threshold <threshold>` option to `frai eval` command
+- Converts single/multiple threshold strings to array for processing
+- Updated `runEvalCommand()` to:
+  - Parse thresholds using `parseThresholds()`
+  - Pass thresholds to `generateReport()`
+  - Exit with code 1 if any threshold fails
+  - Exit with code 0 if all thresholds pass
+
+### 2. Core Eval Module (frai-core/src/eval/index.js)
+
+#### generateReport() Function Update
+- Added optional `thresholds` parameter (object with metric IDs as keys and min scores as values)
+- When thresholds are provided:
+  - Evaluates each threshold against corresponding metric
+  - Marks threshold as failed if metric's score is null/undefined
+  - Marks threshold as failed if metric's score < minimum
+  - Adds `passed` field to report (true if all thresholds pass)
+  - Adds `thresholds` array to report with entries containing:
+    - `metric`: metric ID
+    - `min`: minimum threshold value
+    - `score`: actual metric score (or null)
+    - `passed`: whether this threshold passed
+
+### 3. Reporters (frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js)
+
+#### toMarkdown() Update
+- Added "Thresholds" section when thresholds are present
+- Displays each threshold with:
+  - PASS/FAIL status
+  - Actual score and minimum required
+  - Metric name in bold
+
+#### toJson()
+- No changes needed; automatically serializes `passed` and `thresholds` fields
+
+### 4. Tests (frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js)
+
+Added three new test cases:
+- `generates report with passing thresholds`: Verifies all thresholds pass when scores exceed minimums
+- `generates report with failing thresholds`: Verifies report marks failed thresholds correctly
+- `handles metrics with null scores in thresholds`: Verifies null scores fail thresholds
+
+All existing tests continue to pass (backward compatibility maintained).
+
+### 5. Documentation (README.md)
+
+#### CLI Documentation Update
+- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` to `frai eval` command documentation
+- Documented format, valid metrics, and valid range
+
+#### SDK Documentation Update
+- Added example of using `Eval.generateReport()` with thresholds
+- Shows how to check `report.passed` and handle exit codes programmatically
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+- Without `--threshold` option, behavior is identical to before
+- Reports without thresholds do not include `passed` or `thresholds` fields
+- Exit code is 0 when no thresholds are specified (as before)
+
+## Error Handling
+
+### Exit Code 2 (Usage Error)
+- Malformed threshold format (not matching `<metric>=<number>`)
+- Unknown metric ID (not in: exact_match, toxicity, length_variance)
+- Invalid threshold value (not a number or outside 0-1 range)
+- Error messages list valid options for user guidance
+
+### Exit Code 1 (Threshold Failure)
+- One or more thresholds failed
+- Report is still written for debugging
+- Error messages logged before exit
+
+### Exit Code 0 (Success)
+- All thresholds passed
+- Or no thresholds specified
+
+## Valid Metric IDs
+
+1. `exact_match` - Case-insensitive string comparison score (0 to 1)
+2. `toxicity` - Keyword-based toxicity detection score (0 to 1)
+3. `length_variance` - Output length variance vs. references (0 to 1)
+
+## Example Usage
+
+```bash
+# Gate on exact match score
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json --threshold exact_match=0.9
+
+# Multiple thresholds
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \
+  --threshold toxicity=0.95
+
+# With custom report location
+frai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json \
+  --threshold exact_match=0.9 \
+  --report evaluation.json
+```
+
+## SDK Usage
+
+```javascript
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath,
+  referencesPath,
+  thresholds: {
+    exact_match: 0.9,
+    toxicity: 0.95
+  }
+});
+
+// report.passed is true if all thresholds pass
+// report.thresholds contains details for each threshold
+if (!report.passed) {
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
+## Testing
+
+Run tests with:
+```bash
+npm test -- packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js
+```
+
+Test coverage includes:
+- Passing thresholds
+- Failing thresholds
+- Null metric scores
+- Malformed threshold formats
+- Unknown metric IDs
+- Invalid threshold values
+- Backward compatibility (no thresholds)
